{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And he came up to Hebron.</b> Caleb alone went there and prostrated himself on the graves of the patriarchs, so that he would not be drawn into the plot of his companions, etc. Thus Rashi interpreted. And the reason is that Moses did not pray for him as he did for Joshua. Another interpretation — <b>and he came up to Hebron:</b> it is the way of Scripture to call several spies and scouts in singular language, as it is written: והאורב קם ממקומו." "<b>And there Ahiman.</b> Since they are about to say, וגם ילידי הענק ראינו שם, Scripture specifies for you where they saw them." "<b>And Hebron was built seven years before Zoan of Egypt.</b> And the Nephilim who were there from ancient times had not yet died, and Scripture comes to refute the spies, who are about to say: ארץ אוכלת יושביה היא." "<b>Before Zoan of Egypt.</b> Scripture specifies for you the preeminence of the Land of Israel over the preeminence of the land of Egypt, because they had come out of it and were expert in it and recognized its goodness and its preeminence."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:51.834813797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}